-- Migration: Add asaas_customer_id to patients
-- Talitha Psicologia — Sprint 5 (Financeiro e Asaas)
--
-- Context: the Asaas API requires CPF to create a customer, but Edge
-- Functions don't have the KEK (ADR-0001). The Server Action decrypts
-- CPF and calls manage-asaas-customer, which returns the customer ID.
-- Without a column to store it, the code scans previous charges — O(n),
-- fragile, and fails on the first charge for a new patient.
--
-- Sensitivity: D11 (Interno). asaas_customer_id is an opaque token
-- (cus_...) generated by Asaas. It contains no PII. It does create a
-- cross-reference to Asaas, but exploiting that requires the Asaas
-- API key (separate secret). Same classification as charges.asaas_payment_id,
-- which is stored without encryption. No cipher needed.
--
-- Write access: service_role only (manage-asaas-customer Edge Function).
-- authenticated has NO INSERT/UPDATE on patients (A4 patch). The column
-- is also excluded from GRANT SELECT — the browser client has no need
-- for Asaas internal identifiers.
--
-- Elimination (R20): eliminable. On LGPD deletion request, this field
-- can be set to NULL without affecting local financial records (charges
-- have their own asaas_payment_id). The Asaas-side record is the
-- patient's responsibility to request from Asaas directly.

ALTER TABLE patients ADD COLUMN asaas_customer_id TEXT UNIQUE;
